# Silver Layer (Next Stage, Not Yet Implemented)

Silver is the next implementation stage. This rule defines persistent context only.

## Input

- Consume Bronze Parquet datasets generated by the completed Bronze layer.

## Expected Responsibilities

- Data-quality checks:
  - completeness
  - uniqueness
  - referential integrity
  - business-rule validation
- Data cleansing/transformation as required by assignment artifacts
- Quality status/result handling
- Valid/invalid record handling and outputs as required

## Output Expectations

- Silver datasets suitable for Gold-layer business aggregation.
- Quality outcomes should be explicit and testable.

## Boundaries

- Do not modify completed Data Generation or Bronze behavior while implementing Silver unless explicitly requested.
- Do not invent Silver behaviors not supported by assignment docs or project artifacts.

## Known Ambiguities

- Exact invalid-record handling strategy and quality result representation may need explicit human confirmation if not fully specified in existing artifacts.
- When ambiguous, document assumptions and ask for confirmation instead of silently choosing semantics.
